{
  "about": "verifyWakeWebhook: how a receiver checks a wake the platform POSTed to its wake webhook (PUT /v1/agents/me/wake-webhook), for the dialects whose receiver is code the agent runs: agentchat (Authorization: Bearer <secret>), hermes (X-Webhook-Timestamp + X-Webhook-Signature-V2 = hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, \"<timestamp>.<body>\")) and standard-webhooks (webhook-id / webhook-timestamp / webhook-signature \"v1,<base64 HMAC-SHA256(key, \"<id>.<timestamp>.<body>\")>\", a whsec_ secret is base64-decoded, any other is its UTF-8 bytes; the header may list several space-separated signatures). The body is checked as the exact bytes received; the payload is returned only when it is a JSON object of type agentchat.wake. The standard-webhooks secret is \"whsec_\" followed by standard_webhooks_secret_base64 (built at run time: no secret-shaped literal is committed). Header names are case-insensitive. now is the receiver's clock in unix seconds; tolerance_s is the replay window for the signed dialects.",
